The task is to compute the axis-aligned bounding box of a finite set of points. That is, for a list of (x, y) tuples I have to determine the smallest rectangle whose sides are aligned with the coordinate axes and that contains every point. The six expected answers show a range only of integers, but the specification calls for general numbers, so I must not rely on integer comparisons.

The bounding box is described by its four bounds: the smallest x-coordinate among all the points, the smallest y-coordinate, the largest x-coordinate and the largest y-coordinate. Finding these four is all that is needed, so I can write:

