For this reasoning I follow the standard edge-based approach. Extend each edge into an infinite line, then take the signed cross product of the edge with the next edge to decide which way the turn happens at that vertex. The sign of a cross product is positive for left turns, negative for right turns, and zero when the two edges are colinear. So:

