The main diagonal runs from the top-left to the bottom-right. Its elements are at positions (0, 0), (1, 1), ..., (n - 1, n - 1). The anti-diagonal runs from top-right to bottom-left, and its elements are at positions (0, n - 1), (1, n - 2), ..., (n - 1, 0). Iterating over position i in 0 to n - 1, therefore, gives the element (i, i) on the main diagonal and (i, n - 1 - i) on the anti-diagonal. The only overlapping cell is when i = n - 1 - i, which happens only when n is odd and gives a unique position in the middle of the grid. When the grid has even side length, every element on the two diagonals is distinct.

