        0 & \text{if the cell (i, j) is blocked,} \\
        dp[i-1][j] + dp[i][j-1] & \text{otherwise},
    \end{cases}
$$
where each entry counts the number of paths to that cell. The starting cell, (0, 0), must be open for there to be any paths, and the cell a few steps up or to the left is implicitly 0 when i or j is 0. With board indices running from 0, the paths from cell (i, j) go to (i, j + 1) and (i + 1, j), so I flipped both indices.

