Metaphor in school
Suppose the institution allows students to commute only on certain cars, and a register lists for each day the direction of the car arriving that day. The rule for admission is that northbound and southbound cars reach on even numbered days, while eastbound and westbound reach on odd days, since the schedule starts green for north-south on day 0. For one course day this is true for both arrived cars, which is acceptance, and for three course days it would apply to the indicated days only.

The code counts pointers directly and works for any initial green duration and arrival times, so I present it as a general counter.

At tick 0 the N/S green light begins; then the E/W phase is shown for green_duration ticks, after which N/S comes back for another green_duration ticks, and so on. A car in direction d passes only if d is among N or S while the first phase is on, or among E or W while the second phase is on.

